Description: build the interface with a bundler chain whose native parts have a source
 CoolerControl 5.1.2 builds its Vue interface with Vite 8, whose bundler (Rolldown) and CSS minifier (Lightning CSS) npm delivers as prebuilt
 shared objects that cannot be built without an earlier prebuilt copy. The same interface source builds with Vite 7.3.8 (Rollup 4.68.6, whose
 native part is Rust and is built from its source in this package) and esbuild 0.28.2 (Debian's, ESBUILD_BINARY_PATH), with one change of the build
 configuration (minify and cssMinify use esbuild) and @vitejs/plugin-legacy 7.2.1 (the line for Vite 7). Not a line of the interface's own code or
 of its dependencies' versions changes: package-lock.json changes only in the build tools (vite, @vitejs/plugin-legacy; esbuild and rollup join; the
 Rolldown, Lightning CSS and Oxc entries leave; the esbuild and rollup platform packages are in the lock but are never installed, the build installs
 with --omit=optional).
Author: Daniel Ramos (Capitain Jack) <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Forwarded: not-needed
Origin: vendor
